  "instruction": "Read context files, work through pending tasks, mark complete as you go.\nPause if you hit blockers or need clarification.",
  "context": "Language: zh-CN\nAll artifacts must be written in zh-CN.\nKeep OpenSpec structural headings and SHALL/MUST keywords in English.\nProject: jarde, a pure Rust library-first JVM artifact analysis engine.\nArchitecture reference: JVM_Rust_Engine_Final_Architecture.md.\nKeep the core jarde crate host-agnostic. jarde-cli and any reverse-engine backend\nintegration are thin outward adapters that depend on jarde; the core must not\ndepend on CLI, MCP, or host/backend protocol types.\nP0-P5 and crate layering are archived within their recorded scope; 18 main specs are promoted.\nStage archival is not blanket product completion. The 2026-09-20 completion review found two\nrecovery correctness gaps (nested-expression evaluation position, fallback producer retention);\nclose-recovery-correctness-gaps closed them and is archived with its evidence. Use roadmap.md,\nacceptance.md and the support matrix for the current status. Preserve historical archives.\nThe review of bafdcec (behaviour 85828c4) found task-operation stop propagation gaps;\npreserve-task-operation-stops fixed and archived them at 8586356. The benchmark campaign\nthen found two engine defects, now tracked as bound-recovery-recursion (process abort,\nfixed at 4f62e26) and fix-nested-arithmetic-value (expression grouping in the printer,\nbeing fixed); a third change, clarify-structural-output-planes, records the read-rule\ngaps those findings exposed. optimize-demand-workloads remains an unfinished\ninvestigation program even though its O1 child bound-container-lookup is archived.\nQuery and Decompiler share readers and identities but do not start each other.\nPreserve physical origins and raw facts; distinguish symbolic references,\ndefinition resolution, dispatch, output quality, coverage and execution state.\nDo not execute target code or download target dependencies automatically.\nAll input processing, dependency expansion and output need explicit budgets.\nPrefer maintained libraries that pass our conformance gates; see dependencies.md.\nKeep the smallest complete change. Do not create speculative crates or abstractions.\nFavor long-term architecture; do not maintain backward compatibility by default.\nRecord unrelated architectural debt separately instead of expanding a change.\n",
